      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "<!-- Please search existing issues for potential duplicates before filing yours:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues?q=is%3Aissue\r\n-->\r\n\r\n**Godot version:**\r\n3.1\r\n\r\n**Issue description:**\r\nIt's possible to drop some files onto Godot's window and they get added to the selected directory. Cool. But it seems to work only for resources that can be imported and for fonts. Anything else is just ignored. Not only it's confusing, there's no real reason why this happens (is there?). I mean, if someone drops a file into editor, that person wants it to be in the project. And even if it's accidental, deleting a file isn't a big deal.\r\n\r\nSo is it possible this can be changed?",
